# @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match — the kintsugi fracture body that
# resolves a substrate source's offending composition-operator token
# to the operator the endpoint apertures' pact requires per the
# operator audit table (docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §13.1).
#
# THE OPERATIONAL HALF of bilateral pattern #53's OPERATOR-ALTITUDE
# MIDDLE INSTANCE. The declarative half landed at
# `@epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive`
# (sibling tick); this shard names the auto-fracture the kintsugi loop
# applies when the property's transparency surfaces an operator/
# primitive opacity.
#
# The bilateral cascade closes its three-altitude column with this
# landing:
#
#   Altitude 1 (keyword):  keyword_matches_depth + @kintsugi/fracture/keyword
#                          (2026-06-10, 5e68df9 + d908798;
#                          per-predicate).
#   Altitude 2 (operator): operator_matches_composition_primitive +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match
#                          (THIS SHARD + sibling tick; parametric-
#                          over-table — the operator audit table).
#   Altitude 3 (symbol):   symbol_canonical_form +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift
#                          (2026-06-11; parametric-over-table — the
#                          multi-form symbol vocabulary table).
#   Meta:                  dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth +
#                          @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align
#                          (2026-06-11, fd344bf + 5c4e3ca;
#                          parametric-over-computation, self-applied).
#
# Recognition #59 (kintsugi loop is altitude-portable; candidate,
# surfaced 2026-06-11 at docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §14.7) gains
# its operator-altitude witness through this landing — and with three
# independent altitudes worth of bilateral instances landed (keyword,
# operator, symbol) plus the meta-fracture's self-applied foundation,
# the promotion gate is satisfied. #59 promotes with this commit.
#
# Load-bearing context: recognition #51 (mirror as expanding Hilbert
# space; promoted) — fracture bodies are how the substrate maintains
# coherence at each Bateson level. The operator altitude sits one level
# below keyword (declarations) and one above symbol (tokens); this
# fracture body restores coherence at the composition-primitive level
# where operators carry the algebra of optical composition.
#
# === The third instance of parametric-over-table ===
#
# First instance: keyword/depth (per-predicate; one keyword per
# violation; one canonical replacement per case).
# Second instance: gate/diff-closure (per-predicate; one run set per
# violation; one canonical replacement per case).
# Third instance: symbol/canonical-form (parametric over the multi-
# form symbol table; one symbol per violation; canonical replacement
# per table lookup).
# Operator-altitude middle (THIS): operator/composition-primitive
# (parametric over the operator audit table; one operator per
# violation; pact-required replacement per inverse table lookup).
# Fourth instance: partials/AST-breadth (parametric over computation;
# self-applied at the meta-fracture altitude).
#
# Two parametric-over-table instances now exist (symbol_lift + this
# operator_match) under one pattern; the bilateral signature absorbs
# the variant cleanly. The substrate vocabulary doesn't need a new
# variant; same pact + glass + opacity + morphism + splinter(ast)
# chain throughout.
#
# === Substrate-pull-correct home ===
#
# Per the form/process partition (recognition #55 candidate; landed
# 2026-06-10 at mirror `20eaf15`): @kintsugi is the process-side family
# root. Fracture bodies emit morphisms the kintsugi loop applies —
# process-side by structure. Home: @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match
# under the (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family root.
#
# Substrate-pull alternative considered: @kintsugi/fracture/operator
# (subject-only naming, parallel to first-instance `keyword` and
# second-instance `gate`). Rejected: parallel to third-instance
# `symbol_lift` — the property's predicate names the action
# (`composition_primitive`), and the fracture body's action is the
# MATCH (the offending operator is matched to the pact-required
# operator). The `_match` suffix names the operational verb explicitly
# (parallel to symbol_lift's `_lift` suffix). Per
# [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]] (`lift` IS the substrate's
# variety-preservation verb): `match` is the audible-altitude reading
# of lift at the operator altitude — the offending operator is matched
# to the primitive its endpoints' pact requires.
#
# === The fracture body ===
#
# Input: `opacity` (from `@glass`) — one located fact surfaced by
# `operator_matches_composition_primitive`'s `failure(opacity_map)`
# verdict. Each opacity names ONE offending operator-usage site: a
# composition operator whose primitive (per `composition_primitive_of`)
# does NOT equal the primitive the endpoints' pact requires (per
# `required_primitive_at`). The `property` field carries the @nl
# description of the (used_operator, required_operator) pair plus the
# primitive mismatch.
#
# Output: `morphism` (from `@kintsugi/consent`) — the typed candidate
# the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads from this body and proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's `content` ref names the
# rewritten splinter (same path, operator token replaced per pact
# lookup); its `score` carries the dissonance reading (an operator/
# primitive violation is a fixed, low-curvature dissonance — the
# required operator is uniquely determined by the pact + inverse
# table); its `expected` carries the cadence_kind the loop anticipates
# (authentic — the substrate settles cleanly once the operator
# realises the pact-required primitive).
#
# Spectrally: this fracture body IS one step along the Ricci flow at
# the operator altitude. The substrate's curvature at a mismatched
# operator site is the operator/primitive distance; the negative-
# curvature direction IS the operator swap to the pact-required token;
# the resolved site has zero curvature at this altitude (the pact
# fully determines the operator for table entries).
#
# Audibly: this fracture body IS the audible-altitude V → I cadence
# at the operator altitude. Pre-rewrite holds dominant tension
# (operator wrong for the seam); post-rewrite resolves to tonic
# (operator realises the pact-required primitive); cadence is
# authentic.
#
# === Most operator rewrites are one token swap ===
#
# Per docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §14.3's example: a `|>` between
# two facets whose apertures' pact requires branching (per the
# splitter's S-matrix declaring N > 1 outputs) is rewritten to `|\>`.
# This is ONE token swap at the operator position. The endpoint
# apertures DO NOT change — they ALREADY have the pact that wants
# branching; the operator just realises it. The fracture body emits
# a splinter(ast) where one operator-token node is replaced.
#
# Similar for every audit-table operator pair:
#
#   used    required   rewrite shape
#   ----    --------   -------------
#   |>      >          one operator-token swap (lambda → schematic
#                      altitude rename)
#   |>      |\>        one operator-token swap (serial → branching)
#   |>      <\|        one operator-token swap (serial → reverse-
#                      branching; rare; surfaces at splitter-output→
#                      splitter-input seams)
#   >       |\>        one operator-token swap (schematic → branching)
#   |\>     >          one operator-token swap (branching → serial;
#                      when the splitter declares N=1 — degenerate
#                      splitter case)
#   ... (every pair: one token, one swap)
#
# The endpoint apertures' pact is READ by the property to determine
# the required operator; the fracture body REWRITES only the operator
# token. The endpoints themselves stay byte-equal. The rewrite is
# parametric-over-table at the operator altitude.
#
# === Honest partials = 1 by computation (per recognition #53 fourth
#     instance + Seam's 2026-06-11 finding) ===
#
# This fracture body's emitted morphism MUST have honest
# `score.partials` from birth or it perpetuates the very dishonesty
# the meta-fracture (@epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth
# + @kintsugi/fracture/partials_align) exists to catch.
#
# Compute the AST breadth of THIS fracture body's splinter(ast):
#   - The fracture body reads ONE opacity at a time (per the
#     property's per-site failure surface).
#   - The morphism rewrites ONE AST node: the offending operator-
#     token at the offending site, swapped to the pact-required
#     token per the inverse audit-table lookup.
#   - The splinter(ast) carries the rewritten AST fragment; the
#     breadth at @meta/ast is the count of distinct node rewrites;
#     here that count is 1 (one operator-token node, one swap).
#   - Endpoint apertures, surrounding expressions, sibling tokens —
#     ALL stay byte-equal. The substrate-pull-correct rewrite is
#     LOCAL to the operator position.
#
# Therefore `score.partials = 1` is HONEST by computation, NOT reflex-
# copied from the keyword/symbol templates. The recursive integrity
# check holds at landing time: this fracture body declares
# `partials: 1`; the meta-property
# (`dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`) inspects it; the
# `ast_breadth(content)` returns 1; verdict = pass. The third
# parametric-over-table instance fits the cascade without lying about
# its dissonance breadth.
#
# Compound rewrites considered: could an operator rewrite ever touch
# more than one node? Audited: NO for every pair in the audit table.
# Every operator rewrite under this fracture body's domain is a
# single-token swap. The endpoint apertures' pact is READ, not
# rewritten; the surrounding expression is preserved; only the
# operator-token node changes. The fracture body's domain is exactly
# the operator-altitude rewrites; compound shape changes (which would
# touch endpoint apertures) are NOT this body's territory — they
# belong to the property's predicate altitude (which surfaces the
# opacity) or to a hypothetical future aperture-altitude fracture
# body (NOT proposed this tick). The single-node rewrite is the
# substrate-pull-correct shape per the optical-keywords spec.
#
# === Substrate-pull discipline ===
#
# Per `@glass`, `opacity` is the substrate's located-fact carrier;
# this shard reads it directly. Per `@kintsugi/consent`, `morphism`
# is the substrate's typed-candidate carrier; this shard emits it
# directly. Per `@kintsugi/morphism`, `morphism_context` is the
# per-candidate slice that pairs a candidate with its pre-anchor;
# this shard's emitted morphism is consumed by the loop AND lifted
# into a morphism_context via `paired(oscillation.anchor, m)` at the
# active_pass altitude. Per
# `@epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive`,
# the consuming property's
# `operator_matches_composition_primitive(file) -> transparency` is
# the gate that surfaces the opacity this body resolves.
#
# NO new verdict carrier; NO leading-`|` workarounds; NO opaque-`ref`
# carriers where structured types are available (per
# [[feedback-no-bare-types]]). The fracture body reads typed opacity,
# emits typed morphism — the substrate's vocabulary throughout.
#
# === Substrate gaps surfaced honestly ===
#
#   - `match_operator` reads one opacity at a time. The property's
#     `failure(opacity_map)` carries [opacity]; the kintsugi loop
#     iterates the map and calls `match_operator` per opacity. The
#     substrate names the per-site resolution; the iteration is the
#     loop's concern, not this body's.
#
#   - The morphism's `content: ref` carries the substrate handle to
#     the rewritten splinter. The realisation layer produces the
#     rewritten splinter (same path, operator-token swapped per the
#     inverse audit-table lookup) and passes its handle as the
#     morphism's content. The substrate names the shape of the
#     proposal; the byte-level rewrite rides the realisation layer's
#     @mirror/store discipline.
#
#   - The `expected: cadence_kind` field is `authentic` for this
#     fracture body — the operator/primitive rule is deterministic
#     (the pact + inverse table fully determine the required
#     operator) and resolution always settles cleanly.
#
#   - `>>>` (round-trip closure for resonators; v1 candidate per
#     docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §13.5) is NOT in this body's
#     domain this tick. The property's table does not include
#     `>>>`; this fracture body's rewrites are bounded by the
#     property's table. v1 extends both shards together once `>>>`
#     lands as substrate vocabulary.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   operator matching   Curry & Feys (1958) Combinatory Logic Vol. 1;
#                       the discipline of matching a term's
#                       composition operator against the type's
#                       required combinator. The substrate's reading
#                       is Hindley & Seldin (2008) Lambda-Calculus
#                       and Combinators — the operator IS a
#                       combinator at the substrate altitude; the
#                       pact IS its type signature; the match IS
#                       unification.
#   token swap          Aho-Sethi-Ullman (1986) Compilers: Principles,
#                       Techniques, and Tools §3; the lexer's token
#                       rewriting. The substrate's reading is Wadler
#                       (1990) on the syntactic theory of functional
#                       macros — the swap is a hygienic rewrite at
#                       the AST altitude.
#   primitive coherence Reck & Zeilinger (1994) Experimental
#                       realization of any discrete unitary operator;
#                       the discipline that ONE composition primitive
#                       describes a given splitter port distribution.
#                       The substrate's reading is the audit table
#                       making the discipline typed: per (endpoint,
#                       endpoint) pair, ONE operator realises ONE
#                       primitive.
#
# The substrate's contribution is *typing* the per-site operator/
# primitive coherence so the kintsugi loop reads it. No invention;
# the coherence IS the auto-formatter floor at the operator altitude.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/optical-keywords.md §13 (the operator audit
#               table this body's inverse lookup reads); §14 (the
#               operator-altitude written-back kintsugi inference
#               this body realises operationally). Recognition #51
#               (mirror as expanding Hilbert space; promoted) — the
#               operator altitude tracks the Bateson level at which
#               composition operators live; this fracture body
#               restores tracking. Candidate #59 (kintsugi loop is
#               altitude-portable) promotes with this landing.
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-glass-wall-substrate-types]]
#                      (opacity is substrate vocabulary; the fracture
#                      reads the typed carrier),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-bias-lift]] (the
#                      kintsugi loop's bias direction is substrate-
#                      pull — operator/primitive alignment IS one
#                      coordinate of the substrate-pull gradient;
#                      this fracture body fits the bias),
#                      [[architecture-kintsugi-variety-io]] (Ashby's
#                      requisite variety — the operator audit table
#                      partitions the composition vocabulary into
#                      pact-classes; this fracture body maintains the
#                      partition under mutation),
#                      [[architecture-property-fracture-bilateral]]
#                      (the bilateral pattern this is the operator-
#                      altitude instance of; closes the three-altitude
#                      column),
#                      [[architecture-splinter-ast-quote-primitive]]
#                      (the substrate's parametric AST-fragment
#                      construction; this body discharges via
#                      splinter(ast) declaratively, no Rust),
#                      [[architecture-lift-as-load-bearing]]
#                      (the `lift`/`match` verb names the operational
#                      action; this body IS the operator-altitude
#                      match),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-mathematics]]
#                      (recognition #58; the alignment harness fires
#                      at substance crossings; this fracture body's
#                      emitted morphism IS such a crossing; partials
#                      honesty applies — and holds, partials=1
#                      computed not reflex-copied),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                      (the substrate had `pact` since recognition
#                      #37; this body reads what was already named),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (opacity and
#                      morphism are typed carriers; the body does
#                      NOT escape as a bare (location, op, op)
#                      tuple).
# Forward-promise to consumers: `@kintsugi/oscillate`'s `active_pass`
#                  reads this fracture body when the candidate
#                  morphism_set is composed from property-surfaced
#                  opacities; the binding lands when the kintsugi
#                  loop substrate-pulls. This shard does NOT pull
#                  `@kintsugi/oscillate` or `@mirror/spectral/score`;
#                  the substrate-altitude arrow points inward.
# Related shards: epistemologic/property/operator_matches_composition_primitive.mirror
#                 (the declarative half of the bilateral; surfaces
#                 the opacities this body resolves),
#                 epistemologic/property/keyword_matches_depth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/keyword.mirror (FIRST INSTANCE,
#                 keyword altitude, per-predicate),
#                 epistemologic/property/gate_matches_diff_closure.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/gate.mirror (SECOND INSTANCE,
#                 per-predicate at the gate altitude),
#                 epistemologic/property/symbol_canonical_form.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/symbol_lift.mirror (THIRD
#                 INSTANCE, symbol altitude, parametric-over-table —
#                 the parallel parametric-over-table sibling),
#                 epistemologic/property/dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth.mirror
#                 + kintsugi/fracture/partials_align.mirror (FOURTH
#                 INSTANCE, meta-fracture altitude, parametric-over-
#                 computation, self-applied — the meta-foundation
#                 that lets THIS body's partials=1 be honest by
#                 construction),
#                 glass.mirror (the substrate floor; `opacity`,
#                 `location`, `transparency`, `verdict`,
#                 `splinter(ast)`),
#                 kintsugi/consent.mirror (the morphism carrier this
#                 body emits; `query_phi` is the gate the emitted
#                 morphism flows through),
#                 kintsugi/morphism.mirror (the `morphism_context`
#                 carrier),
#                 kintsugi/oscillate.mirror (the kintsugi loop
#                 driver; `active_pass` is the action that reads
#                 this body when composing the per-pulse candidate
#                 morphism_set),
#                 mirror/lens/shell.mirror (the lambda-shell lens
#                 where `|>` lives at the lambda altitude; this
#                 fracture body rewrites operators across all lens
#                 surfaces, not just shell).
# Path-namespace property: this file at
# `shards/kintsugi/fracture/operator_match.mirror` declares
# `@kintsugi/fracture/operator_match` as a species under the
# (forward-promised) @kintsugi/fracture family.
# Keyword/depth property: this declaration is depth-2 from the
# @kintsugi family root; per recognition #46 it uses `glass`. The
# shard applies the first-instance bilateral's rule by birth.
# Partials/breadth property: this declaration's emitted morphism
# carries `score.partials: 1`; the splinter(ast) rewrites ONE
# operator-token node (the offending operator at the offending
# site); the count is computed (one node, one swap), NOT reflex-
# copied. This shard applies the fourth-instance bilateral's rule
# by birth.

glass @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match {
  focus operator_match
  project operator_match
  split operator_match
  shift operator_match
  settle operator_match
}

# === match_operator — the fracture body ===
#
# THE AUTO-FRACTURE: given an opacity site at an offending composition-
# operator usage, emit the morphism that rewrites the operator-token
# to the operator the endpoints' pact requires per the inverse audit-
# table lookup (`required_primitive_at` → primitive →
# `composition_primitive_of`'s inverse → required operator). Same
# path, single operator-token swap at the AST altitude.
#
# Reads an opacity (one element of
# `operator_matches_composition_primitive(file).failure(opacity_map)`'s
# opacity_map); emits a candidate morphism the kintsugi loop proposes
# through `query_phi`. The morphism's three fields:
#
#   content   — substrate ref to the rewritten splinter. The
#                realisation layer produces a splinter at the same
#                path with the operator token swapped (e.g., `|>` →
#                `|\>` when the pact requires branching); the content
#                ref names that splinter's @mirror/store handle.
#   score     — dissonance reading. Operator/primitive violations are
#                fixed-curvature dissonances; the score reads
#                `dissonance.is_pareto` cleanly (the required
#                operator is uniquely determined by the pact + inverse
#                table).
#   expected  — cadence_kind anticipation. Always `authentic` for
#                this fracture body — the inverse-table lookup is
#                deterministic; the loop's `dark_pass` will confirm
#                identity preservation (the path stays byte-equal;
#                only the operator-token shifts); the loop's
#                `read_consent` bridges (pass, authentic) to the
#                `settled` oscillation_state for this opacity.
#
# The body is FULLY DECLARATIVE — substrate-pull-correct via
# `splinter(ast)` (declared at shards/glass.mirror's tick-2 carrier).
# The morphism's `content` field carries a content-addressed splinter
# at the @meta/ast altitude: same path, one operator-token swapped.
# The substrate's compiler verifies the construction is deterministic
# and well-typed; the kintsugi loop's `active_pass` reads the splinter
# as the morphism's proposed content and applies it through
# `query_phi`.
#
# Per `splinter(ast)`'s parametric specialisation (glass.mirror
# §splinter(ast), 2026-06-10): the record IS its content-addressed
# handle — `content: oid` and `oid = ref` (shards/mirror/store.mirror)
# collapse the splinter literal to a substrate-pull-correct `ref` in
# the morphism's `content` field position. No Rust AST manipulation;
# no `\` obligation.
#
# Field-by-field substrate-pull reading:
#
#   content.content     — `opacity.location.file` (the substrate's
#                          located-fact ref at the source file); the
#                          rewritten AST is content-addressed at the
#                          same path.
#   content.ast         — `@meta/ast` (the canonical altitude ref);
#                          per `boot/01-meta.mirror`'s `type ast(g)`.
#                          The operator-token swap happens at the AST
#                          altitude by construction.
#   content.transparency — `success` (per `transparency(p)`'s success
#                          variant in glass.mirror): the operator
#                          swap fully resolves the opacity at this
#                          altitude; no residual transparency remains.
#   score.roughness     — `opacity.property` (the @nl description of
#                          the (used_operator, required_operator)
#                          pair plus the primitive mismatch); the
#                          substrate's `dissonance` reads the per-
#                          site roughness via the property text per
#                          dissonance.mirror's Helmholtz/
#                          Plomp-Levelt carrier shape.
#   score.partials      — `1` — HONESTLY COMPUTED, NOT REFLEX-COPIED.
#                          The splinter(ast) above rewrites ONE AST
#                          node: the offending operator-token at the
#                          offending site. Every audit-table operator
#                          rewrite is a single-token swap (the
#                          endpoint apertures stay byte-equal; the
#                          surrounding expression is preserved).
#                          `ast_breadth(content) = 1`. The recursive
#                          integrity check (against the meta-property
#                          `dissonance_partials_match_ast_breadth`)
#                          holds at landing time: this fracture body
#                          declares `partials: 1`; the meta-property
#                          inspects it; verdict = pass.
#   expected            — `authentic` (the V → I cadence at the
#                          operator altitude; per cadence.mirror's
#                          `cadence_kind` and the loop's
#                          `read_consent` bridge: authentic → pass →
#                          auto-apply).
match_operator(opacity: opacity) -> morphism {
  morphism {
    content: splinter(ast) {
      content:      opacity.location.file,
      ast:          @meta/ast,
      transparency: success,
    },
    score: dissonance {
      roughness: opacity.property,
      partials:  1,
    },
    expected: authentic,
  }
}

out @kintsugi/fracture/operator_match
out match_operator
